WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:04.090
From the very opening scene of "The Batman,"
new villain the Riddler enacts a murderous

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:08.060
and effective campaign of terror to expose
the corruption at the heart of Gotham City.

00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:11.490
The frightening villain first targets city
officials while leaving a series of riddles

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:15.790
chock-full of clues for Batman to uncover
the conspiracy that has turned Gotham rotten.

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:19.840
In fact, Riddler later tells an appalled Batman
that he was inspired by the Caped Crusader's

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:24.310
own use of violence in crafting his plans
to permanently change the city and its infrastructure.

00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:27.900
The Riddler is eventually captured, but Batman
is too late to work out the final part of

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:28.900
his plan.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:32.410
After the Riddler's car bombs destroy the
breakwaters of Gotham, flooding the downtown

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:36.790
area, his followers intend to kill mayor-elect
Bella Reàl and shoot into the crowd of people

00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:38.630
taking refuge in the stadium.

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:42.789
Batman and Catwoman are forced to fight the
Riddler's devotees and save the city residents.

00:00:42.789 --> 00:00:47.320
Fans praised how the early stages of the Riddler's
master plan felt but were very split over

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:48.899
his scheme in the last act.

00:00:48.899 --> 00:00:49.899
Here's why.

00:00:49.899 --> 00:00:53.870
In a discussion of "The Batman" in the r/movies
subreddit, some superhero fans were frustrated

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:58.420
by how nonsensical the Riddler's endgame is
compared to what one user called, quote, "[his]

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:02.269
(brilliant) plan to publicly embarrass, expose,
and assassinate the city's leadership" earlier

00:01:02.269 --> 00:01:03.269
in the movie.

00:01:03.269 --> 00:01:06.590
The Riddler did tell his devotees that he
wanted real change enacted in Gotham.

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:10.740
But creating a major disaster via bombing
Gotham's sea walls, and then using that flood

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:15.189
to kill mayor-elect Bella Reàl is not on
par with the string of killings Riddler masterminded

00:01:15.189 --> 00:01:16.189
earlier in the movie.

00:01:16.189 --> 00:01:19.060
The same redditor also noticed that the mayhem
didn't even make sense.

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:20.060
They wrote,

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:23.350
"The plan was to get everyone in the stadium
and have like 10 guys in masks snipe everyone?

00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:25.070
Why not just blow up the building?"

00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:28.649
The scheme seems like it'd be too easy for
someone like Batman to foil compared to the

00:01:28.649 --> 00:01:31.039
destructive power of a bomb or another device.

00:01:31.039 --> 00:01:34.210
It's understandable, then, that some fans
took issue with the Riddler expanding his

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:38.140
lethal crusade to ordinary citizens instead
of just corrupt city officials.

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:41.710
Part of the issue is that, unlike "Batman
Begins," which involves the villain tampering

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:45.650
with Gotham's water supply in the final act,
the destruction of Gotham's sea wall isn't

00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:48.170
foreshadowed or telegraphed to the audience
at all.

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:49.780
One Reddit user noticed that, writing,

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:53.689
"...at no point in the movie are we ever told
about a sea wall keeping Gotham dry.

00:01:53.689 --> 00:01:57.390
Suddenly ... [The Riddler is] blowing up dikes
to drown the city and wash everything away."

00:01:57.390 --> 00:02:01.359
It's worth noting that there were some passing
references to the seawall - like hidden on

00:02:01.359 --> 00:02:05.170
Riddler's floor map and in newspaper clippings,
so you would've had to pay attention to the

00:02:05.170 --> 00:02:07.159
small details to figure out the clues.

00:02:07.159 --> 00:02:10.979
The flooding also doesn't feel consistent
with the tone of the dark, stripped-down film.

00:02:10.979 --> 00:02:14.290
Compared to the detective story at the heart
of "The Batman," the last 30 minutes are more

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:18.530
of the climax to what feels like a standard,
action-packed superhero blockbuster.

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:22.700
One Reddit user wrote that, in their opinion,
"the final act was needlessly dramatic compared

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:25.580
to the rest of the movie that felt pretty
grounded until that point."

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:29.540
However, other Redditors pointed out that
the final scenes help complete Batman's arc.

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:33.000
Throughout "The Batman," the titular hero
often comes off more like a movie monster

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:34.250
than a superhero.

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:38.380
Batman is obsessed with the "Gotham Project,"
and as Bella Reàl observes, isn't doing much

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:40.390
to help the population when he's Bruce Wayne.

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:43.170
"You really could be doing more for this city.

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:47.470
Your family has a history of philanthropy,
but near as I can tell, you're not doing anything."

00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:51.170
But when Batman saves the innocent folks trapped
in the flooded downtown arena, this leads

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:55.040
Mayor Reál and the helpless citizens to trust
him enough to lead them out of the flood.

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:59.540
He also recognizes that the Riddler shooters
are traumatized, angry people, much like himself.

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:03.980
One Redditor argued that "seeing Batman evolve
as a hero through those scenes [was] crucial".

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:07.620
Additionally, Bruce empathizes with the people
he rescues as well as the shooters.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:11.190
In the end, Batman decides that he can't only
personify "vengeance" but should also be an

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:14.700
inspiration to the residents of Gotham who
just survived a terrifying event.

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:18.730
Arguably, "The Batman" could have had a different
climax, but it might not have delivered the

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:20.810
same emotional payoff.

